A||||6||Raydar||4.10 4 speed w/V-6 question||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||02-04-2000||11:41 AM||||Friend of mine has an 86 V-6 4-speed car. Wants to install the 4.10 4-speed from an 84 4-cyl. Do they use the same clutch, release bearing, fork, and slave? Do you have to use the 4-cyl stuff? Anyone familiar with this swap? <BR>Several searches didn't turn up anything meaningful. Any help will be greatly appreciated. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||02-04-2000||12:36 PM||||Ed Parks has this setup on his 85SE.  Write to him at<BR>Fierofactory@juno.com<P>or call him at  (256) 420-5391<P>I've driven the car and it is very peppy.  BTW, he actually gets the same gas mileage at 70 mph as I do with my 85SE v-6 with the Muncie 4 spd.  Apparently the 4.10 gears makes the car run in a very good power band at that speed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||02-04-2000||01:19 PM||||Keith Huff of Fiero Motorsports has 4.10 in his 3.4 V6. He took the 4.10 final gear out of a 4 cyl tranny case and put it in the V6 tranny case. The V6 case is built a little bit more stronger than the other. We have seen one 4 cyl tranny case on a a stock V6 break the case. <BR>Be advised though, freeway speeds really make the engine scream and the gas mileage will suffer. I spend my life on the freeways so this would be foolish for me. But off the line you GO!||||reg||10
Z||000003||Raydar||02-04-2000||10:47 PM||||Thanks, guys!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||02-06-2000||08:32 AM||||have that setup in my 86 GT,  410 in the v-6,  <BR>Use all the v-6 stuff! <BR>My rpms i think is about 400rpms more at 65 than it use to be!  <BR>but is a demon off the line! and through all the gears.<BR>(sorry...... W.ThornIII:~)  <BR>I can nail it at 10 mph in first gear and smoke em real nice! <BR>Car goes down the road at a 45 degree angle LOL  (only once before winter on 70 degree pavement ) <BR>because i never abuse a car!!   <BR>Well wait a sec...... i had an escort parts hauler that.......well that's another tale!<BR>FD<p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 02-06-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000005||Raydar||02-06-2000||07:17 PM||||Thanks, Dave. I'll pass it along. He's already got the 4.10 sitting in a corner of his garage. I'll let y'all know how it turns out. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||02-07-2000||02:06 AM||||Okay, Dave (or anybody else)...<BR>Did you keep your same shift and select cables? Or did you have to use the ones specific to the 84? (I'm told that the part #s are different. Haven't verified.) TIA!<BR>Steve||||reg||1
